(7510596, 1198526, 167587, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> This is such a wonderful photo, but it''s not a silhouette at all. I don''t buy into the fact that a silhouette has to be completely black, but there''s just way too much detail for it to be a silhouette. Kudos on the shot. I like that you left the word tracks on the sign showing. But it just doesn''t fit the challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The image is "high key," and I agree it borders on being a silhouette. I kinda knew that it was really pushing it when I entered it in the challenge. I too thought the shot was interesting,  and the that just maybe I could get away with the entry. For me, the low score from the challenge doesn''t take away from the image itself. Thanks for your comments and response!</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: This is such a wonderful photo, but it''s not a silhouette at all. I don''t buy into the fact that a silhouette has to be completely black, but there''s just way too much detail for it to be a silhouette. Kudos on the shot. I like that you left the word tracks on the sign showing. But it just doesn''t fit the challenge.   The image is "high key," and I agree it borders on being a silhouette. I kinda knew that it was really pushing it when I entered it in the challenge. I too thought the shot was interesting,  and the that just maybe I could get away with the entry. For me, the low score from the challenge doesn''t take away from the image itself. Thanks for your comments and response!', '2017-04-24 13:24:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7510599, 1198244, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> Some people might be overly harsh and think that it''s not enough of a silhouette on the right (but then again, my screen is a tad bright, I think, so it may be better on other screens. But the man with the cane is great and I like the difference in size. I''m wishing there was a vignette just to take the edges down a bit to add more moodiness. Nice find! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hmmm.... Wendy must have a very bright monitor....<br/> <br/>Looks like you''re on team Posthumous this time around! 9 from me.</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: Some people might be overly harsh and think that it''s not enough of a silhouette on the right (but then again, my screen is a tad bright, I think, so it may be better on other screens. But the man with the cane is great and I like the difference in size. I''m wishing there was a vignette just to take the edges down a bit to add more moodiness. Nice find!   hmmm.... Wendy must have a very bright monitor.... Looks like you''re on team Posthumous this time around! 9 from me.', '2017-04-24 13:40:35.000000', NULL, 0),
